@startuml inputs
' Hand-maintained. Source of truth = the workflow_call blocks of master-java-pipeline.yml, java-verify.yml, java-release.yml
' and the identical input trio at the top of every leaf workflow.
title Input, secret and permission plumbing — what an added input costs

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

package "consumer caller" as C #EEEEEE {
  [with: / secrets:] as W
  [permissions:] as P <<unset = none>>
}

package "master-java-pipeline.yml — the public API" as M #FFFFFF {
  [java-version · cache-type] as SHARED
  [build-egress-policy] as BEP
  [release-egress-policy] as REP
  [extra-build-endpoints] as EB
  [extra-test-endpoints] as ET
  [extra-security-endpoints] as ES
  [extra-docker-endpoints] as ED
  [extra-gitops-endpoints] as EG
  [spring-boot-args · test-args] as ARGS
  [gitops-manifest-path] as GMP
  [signer-identity-regexp] as SIR
}

package "grouping layer\njava-verify.yml / java-release.yml" as GRP #E6F4EA {
  [re-declares every input] as RD
  [narrows permissions per job] as NP
}

package "leaf workflow — the egress trio" as LEAF #E8F0FE {
  [egress-policy] as EP <<default "block">>
  [allowed-endpoints] as AE <<base allowlist lives HERE,\nas the input's default>>
  [extra-allowed-endpoints] as XAE <<appended; base stays intact>>
}

W --> SHARED
W --> BEP
W --> REP
P --> NP : intersects

BEP --> RD
REP --> RD
EB --> RD
ET --> RD
ES --> RD
ED --> RD
EG --> RD
ARGS --> RD
GMP --> RD
SIR --> RD
SHARED --> RD

RD --> EP
RD --> XAE
NP --> LEAF

note right of AE
  harden-runner receives:
    allowed-endpoints
    + extra-allowed-endpoints
  A host EVERY consumer needs belongs
  in this default. A consumer-specific
  host belongs in their extra-* input.
end note

note bottom of M
  **Adding an input is a 3-file edit** — leaf,
  grouping layer, master — and it is a breaking
  change for old pins: a consumer passing an
  input their pinned SHA does not declare fails
  with "invalid input".

  A **renamed** workflow file is worse: it fails
  with "workflow was not found", and only once the
  consumer bumps their pin — detached from the cause.
end note

note left of M
  **master-python-pipeline.yml has the identical
  shape**, differing only in these inputs:
    java-version · cache-type
      → python-version · cache-type
    (new) requirements · dev-requirements
    spring-boot-args → pack-args
    (new) builder-image
  The egress trio, test-args, gitops-manifest-path
  and signer-identity-regexp are verbatim the same.

  Deliberately ABSENT there: python-security.yml
  takes no python-version/cache-type — CodeQL runs
  build-mode "none" and nothing in it runs an
  interpreter. Do not add inputs nothing reads.
end note

note bottom of NP
  **permissions intersect at every level.**
  A reusable workflow can never exceed what the
  caller granted, and an unset permission is
  none — a missing id-token: write silently
  breaks keyless signing.
  Widening a leaf ⇒ widen grouping ⇒ widen
  master ⇒ widen the consumer's caller.
end note

note top of C
  Optional secrets, all falling back to github.token:
  • CR_PAT        — GHCR push + cleanup
  • GITOPS_PAT    — manifest push
  • extra-secrets — JSON object → env vars for
    integration tests; github_token is filtered
    out. Never pass toJSON(secrets).
end note

